  "body": "Stacked on #3478 (merge #3478 first). This PR adds two commits on top of the #3478 head (`f9b38a9d7`).\n\n## What changed\n- New manifest flag `uprightReturn = true`. It says: the script retracts to a safe height and commands the rotaries to zero at the start of each section that follows a tilted section.\n- New engine pass `crates/post/src/post/upright_after_tilt.rs`. `engine::run_program_with` calls it before the hooks.\n  - It tracks the modal A/B/C from the last move that states them.\n  - It finds the first section whose first move states no A/B/C, after a section that left a rotary off zero.\n  - If the script does not declare the flag, the engine adds one counted warning. The warning names the two operations and the flag. A warning blocks the post in the app.\n  - A C angle of C-axis live-tool work (`PARAM LiveTool`) does not count as a tilt. That law is section-scoped (#33).\n- `fanuc.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`, `mach4.cps` and `tormach.cps` declare the flag.\n- The Mach4 AC trunnion fixture moved from `mach4_trunnion.rs` to the shared module `crates/post/tests/ac_trunnion_support/mod.rs`. No test of `mach4_trunnion.rs` changed.\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` lists and explains the flag.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3477-upright-after-tilt-flag.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- `post::dump` writes no angle on a move without a leaning axis. The angle words are modal.\n- Only the script can command the return. #3478 makes the Fanuc and Doosan posts do it. Tormach and Mach4 already did it.\n- No law made a script of the user (`PostRef::File`) do it. Such a script posted an upright operation after a tilted operation at the old lean, and no check stopped it.\n\n## Name of the flag\nThe issue gives `uprightAfterTilt` as an example name. #3478 already defines a script function `uprightAfterTilt()` in `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps`. A top-level `uprightAfterTilt = true` replaces that function, and the post fails with `TypeError: not a callable function`. Thus the flag is `uprightReturn`.\n\n## Tests\nNew pins in `camcraft-post` `upright_after_tilt`:\n- `a_script_without_upright_after_tilt_is_refused_by_name`: a copy of fanuc and doosan-dnm without the flag, tilted then upright, tool 1 and tool 2. Red before the fix: yes (`fanuc (tool 1): the engine refuses the upright section by name: []`).\n- `each_shipped_rotary_post_declares_upright_after_tilt`: fanuc, doosan-dnm, mach4, tormach. Red before the fix: yes.\n- `a_script_without_upright_after_tilt_posts_a_program_with_no_return_to_state`: no refusal for tilted only, tilted then tilted, upright then tilted, upright then upright.\n- `mach4_states_upright_after_an_indexed_section` (issue item 4): retract, then `A0`, then the first X/Y traverse. It passes on unchanged code. Mach4 already did the return; this pins it.\n\nUnit tests in `post::upright_after_tilt::tests`: the refusal text, a table C left off zero, a stated zero, a live-tool C, a re-stated tilt.\n\nMutations:\n- `engine.rs` from base (no call): `a_script_without_upright_after_tilt_is_refused_by_name` is red. Restored: green.\n- `fanuc.cps` from base (no flag): `each_shipped_rotary_post_declares_upright_after_tilt` and the two Fanuc posting pins are red (refused by the new law). Restored: green.\n\nGates on the final head:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base base-3478`: 226 steps, 1 failed. The failed step is `app suites: example_catalog` (`catalog_multiaxis_indexed::regenerates` and `::rebuilds`). This failure comes from #3478, not from this PR:\n  - The regenerated `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc` adds `G91 G28 Z0` / `G90` / `G00 A0.` after `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` in the sections \"Back pocket\" and \"Tilted pocket\". That is the return block of `uprightAfterTilt()` from #3478.\n  - This PR adds only a manifest line to `fanuc.cps`. Fanuc declares the flag, so the new law adds no warning and no line.\n  - I reported it on #3478. The catalog `.nc` must move in #3478 (or in this PR when #3478 asks for it).\n- All other steps pass. These include the post suites `upright_after_tilt`, `mach4_trunnion`, `post_engine`, `fanuc_post`, `doosan_dnm_post` and the app suite `conformance`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. The flag line is a manifest line; no hook output changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The app post gate in a GUI session with a user post. The engine warning is the path that `posting.rs` already blocks on.\n- A real control.\n- A stream from an outside `.cnc` producer whose tilted section states its angle only after its first move. The law refuses such a section after a tilt when the flag is absent. That is the safe side.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #3478: this PR is stacked on it (`fanuc.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`, `upright_after_tilt.rs`).\n- #3471 touches `fanuc.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`, `mach4.cps`, `tormach.cps` and `post/mod.rs`. Different functions and lines (this PR adds one manifest line in each post and one `mod` line). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3483 touches `tormach.cps` (manifest line 26 and other functions). Different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3046 touches `engine.rs`, `post/mod.rs` and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`. Different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3468, #3441 touch `fanuc.cps` in other functions. #3312 touches `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` in another section.\n\nChangelog: A post script that does not declare `uprightReturn = true` is now refused by name when an operation with no stated rotary angles follows a tilted operation, so a user's own post can no longer cut an upright operation with the axes still tilted.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3477\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
